Hand-annotated golden set lives here (30 videos across genres per
RECUT_SPEC.md sec 12: talking head, product, dance/trend, text-heavy
tutorial, cinematic b-roll). Do not commit actual third-party video files
into git - store references/hashes here and pull media from ingest/cache
at eval time (see DESIGN_NOTES.md "Golden set storage").

Layout convention (create when Phase 1 starts):
  eval/golden/<video_id>/source.ref          (URL or hash, not the file)
  eval/golden/<video_id>/project_file.ref    (optional - if this video was
                                               annotated via an editor
                                               project file donation
                                               instead of/alongside hand
                                               scrubbing, a note on how to
                                               re-obtain the .fcpxml/
                                               Premiere-XML/.otio file.
                                               Never commit the project
                                               file itself - same posture
                                               as the video, see below -
                                               it routinely embeds the
                                               donor's local file paths
                                               and OS username)
  eval/golden/<video_id>/annotations.json    (ground truth, matching a
                                               subset of the EditTrace
                                               shape: cut times, transition
                                               types, text layer
                                               timing/strings)

annotations.json can come from two paths (see DESIGN_NOTES.md sec 16,
INSTRUCTIONS.md Unit 0.3/Unit 0.4):
  1. Hand-scrubbing the video frame-by-frame (Unit 0.3's original method -
     still required when no project file exists).
  2. eval/golden/import_project_file.py (Unit 0.4) parsing an editor
     project file (FCPXML / Premiere's "Final Cut Pro XML" export / .otio)
     via OpenTimelineIO, when a donor has one - gives exact cut timestamps
     and transition boundaries in minutes instead of hours; still needs a
     human "second look-through" against the video before it counts (Unit
     0.3's done-criterion, unchanged). CapCut and After Effects project
     files are explicitly out of scope for path 2 - see DESIGN_NOTES.md
     sec 16.4 - donors with only those should go through path 1 instead.

Path 2 adds two fields to each entry in `cuts[]` beyond the original
`{t, type}` shape:
  - source: "project_file" | "cv_detected" | "human_annotated"
  - type_confidence: "exact" | "heuristic" | "fallback_cut"
    (only meaningful when source == "project_file" - see Unit 0.4;
    "fallback_cut" means the importer could not identify the real
    transition type and defaulted to "cut" - treat as needing a human
    check, not as verified ground truth, before trusting it for
    eval/metrics.py's transition_type_accuracy()).
Entries from path 1 (pure hand annotation) omit these fields or set
source: "human_annotated" - eval code must treat their absence as
"human_annotated" for backward compatibility with videos annotated before
Unit 0.4 existed.

text_layers[] entries gain an optional `source` field the same way
("project_file_heuristic" when derived from an overlay-track clip name
via Unit 0.4 - box/font/style stay null in that case and the string/
timing should still be spot-checked, it is not equivalent to OCR'd +
hand-verified ground truth).

A project-file-derived annotation may also include a top-level
`candidate_beat_grid_s` (from OTIO markers, if any were present on the
timeline) - this is NOT the same field as `beat_grid_s` and must not be
auto-promoted into it; a human confirms against the actual audio first.
